<title>NETHERLANDS: Akzo Nobel invests in Indonesian plant.</title>
<headline>Akzo Nobel invests in Indonesian plant.</headline>
<dateline>ARNHEM, Netherlands 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chemical group Akzo Nobel NV said on Monday it had started construction of a $45 million carbon disulfide production unit near the Indonesian capital, Jakarta.</p>
<p>Carbon disulfide is used in the production of viscose textiles, which is a rapidly expanding sector in the Asia-Pacific region, the Dutch group said in a statement.</p>
<p>The plant will employ about 45 people and is expected to come on stream in 1999.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
